<title>INDIA: India Sona up 10 pct, partner hikes stake.</title>
<headline>India Sona up 10 pct, partner hikes stake.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Sona Steering Systems jumped 5.25 rupees, or ten percent, to 60.0 rupees on Friday on news that the company plans to issue equity to its Japanese partner at a price of about 90 rupees per share, traders said.  </p>
<p>About 2,400 shares changed hands in afternoon trade, dealers said, but the shares were held in check by a circuit-breaker as the sharp rally reached a ten percent limit.</p>
<p>Koyo Seiko, Sona's Japanese partner, will have an enhanced equity stake of 20.5 percent following the planned share issue against 8.5 percent at present, Sona's managing director Surinder Kapoor told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;A total of 1.2 million shares will be issued at a price of somewhere around 90 rupees per share,&quot; Kapoor added.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
